  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A good number is a positive integer which is not divisible by the cube (third power) of any prime. For example, 222, 333, 25=5⋅525 = 5 \\cdot 525=5⋅5, 63=7⋅963 = 7 \\cdot 963=7⋅9 and 2057=11⋅11⋅172057 = 11 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 172057=11⋅11⋅17 are good numbers, but 8=2⋅2⋅28 = 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 28=2⋅2⋅2, 9317=7⋅11⋅11⋅119317 = 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 119317=7⋅11⋅11⋅11 and 2401=7⋅7⋅7⋅72401 = 7 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 72401=7⋅7⋅7⋅7 are not good numbers.\n\nA pair of positive integers (x,y)(x, y)(x,y) is special if x⋅yx \\cdot yx⋅y is a good number. A set of positive integers is nice if each pair of different integers from this set is special. In particular, the empty set is nice.\n\nYou are given a set of integers {A1,A2,…,AN}\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N\\}{A1​,A2​,…,AN​}. Find the number of nice subsets of this set.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤401 \\le N \\le 401≤N≤40",
      "1≤Ai≤1081 \\le A_i \\le 10^81≤Ai​≤108 for each valid iii",
      "A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ are pairwise distinct"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the number of nice subsets.",
    "notes": [],
